	if (issuanceOutcomeUnknown) {
		return internalLocalIssueFailure("issuance-rejected", "v3 local issue transaction outcome is unknown");
	}
	return capacityRejected
		? localIssueFailure("graph-rejected", "v3 local issue graph is at capacity")
		: ...
}
```

Confirmed: the diff moved the generic `issuanceOutcomeUnknown` return **below** the terminal block, so a started terminal transaction now returns the latched `"outcome-unknown"` result first. The generic failure still exists for nonterminal ambiguity (6438-6440), and the admission-halt latch (6428-6430) is unchanged and still fires for both paths before either return.

## 5. `issueAuthorFence` — v3-live.ts:6584-6628

```ts
if (settlementProfileFor(registration.payload.trust.trust.profileId) !== "v1") {
	return localIssueFailure("malformed-input", "v3 local issue operation is unknown");
}
...
let plan;
try {
	plan = copySettlementPlan(
		await registration.issuanceStore.readSettlementPlan(registration.issuanceScope),
		registration.issuanceScope
	);
} catch {
	registration.operationAdmissionHalted = true;
	return localIssueFailure("issuance-rejected", "v3 author fence plan read failed");
}
if (
	plan === undefined ||
	plan.fenceSequence !== null ||
	plan.entries.some((entry) => entry.disposition === "manual-review")
) {
	return localIssueFailure("issuance-rejected", "v3 author fence requires a complete durable plan");
}
```

Confirmed: `copySettlementPlan` runs before any property access; the comparison changed from `plan === null` to `plan === undefined` (matching the copy function's fail-closed return). Semantics: store read throws → admission halted + `issuance-rejected`; absent/malformed/wrong-scope plan → `copySettlementPlan` returns undefined → `issuance-rejected`; plan with non-null fenceSequence or any `manual-review` entry → `issuance-rejected`. Only a complete, in-scope, unfenced, fully-decided plan proceeds to `issueOneVertex` with `{ kind: "fence" }`.

## 6. `rebaseIntents` / `validRebaseRow` — v3-live.ts:6757-6776, 6798-6807

```ts
// rebaseIntents
if (
	isControlOperation(sourceOperation, payload.trust.trust.profileId) ||
	(typeof action === "string" &&
		isReservedBatchAction(action) &&
		settlementProfileFor(payload.trust.trust.profileId) !== "v1" &&
		action !== "causalJoin" &&
		action !== "join")
) {
	return ObjectFreeze([]);
}
```

Confirmed: for legacy profiles, `join`/`causalJoin` are exempted from the reserved-action empty-intent path and fall through to `detachedCanonicalOperation` to produce real reconstructed intents; other reserved actions (`acl`, `applicationBatch` handled earlier, fence) still yield empty intents. For settlement v1, `isControlOperation` catches join/causalJoin/fence → control-only (empty intents). `validRebaseRow` (6768-6775) keeps `settlementSourceControl` gated on profile v1. Observation (not a defect): under settlement v1 a non-control reserved action such as a plain `acl` op passes neither branch and produces a real intent — this matches `validRebaseRow`'s explicit `displacedAction === "acl"` allowance, i.e. intentional replay of settlement ACLs.

## 7. `copySettlementPlan` — packages/issuance-store/src/contract.ts:327-356

```ts
export function copySettlementPlan(value: unknown, scope: DurableIssueScope): SettlementPlan | undefined {
	if (
		!isClosedDurableIssuanceRecord(value, ["entries", "fenceSequence", "revision", "scope"]) ||
		!Array.isArray(value.entries) ||
		!isValidDurableAuthorSequence(value.revision) ||
		(value.fenceSequence !== null && !isValidDurableAuthorSequence(value.fenceSequence))
	) {
		return undefined;
	}
	try {
		assertDurableIssueScope(value.scope);
	} catch {
		return undefined;
	}
	if (!durableIssueScopesEqual(value.scope, scope)) return undefined;
	const entries: SettlementPlanEntry[] = [];
	let prior = -1;
	for (const rawEntry of value.entries) {
		const entry = copySettlementPlanEntry(rawEntry);
		if (entry === undefined || entry.sourceSequence <= prior) return undefined;
		entries.push(entry);
		prior = entry.sourceSequence;
	}
	return {
		entries,
		fenceSequence: value.fenceSequence,
		revision: value.revision,
		scope: copyDurableIssueScope(scope),
	};
}
```

Fail-closed and fully detaching: exact closed-record key sets (extra keys reject via `isClosedDurableIssuanceRecord`), per-entry validation (`copySettlementPlanEntry`, 299-319) copies `sourceDigest` bytes via `copyDurableIssuanceBytes`, enforces strictly increasing `sourceSequence`, validates scope and requires scope equality with the caller's scope, and rebuilds the result from fresh objects (`copyDurableIssueScope(scope)`) — getters/accessors/prototype tricks on the input cannot escape into the output. Malformed/absent/wrong-scope → `undefined`.

**Pre-existing export confirmed**: `git log -S 'export function copySettlementPlan'` attributes it to 9fef8d24 (`feat(issuance-store): persist settlement plans atomically`), and `git merge-base --is-ancestor 9fef8d24 e07f8a94` returns true. So e07f8a94 needed no production change outside v3-live.ts — it only added `copySettlementPlan` to the value-import list (v3-live.ts:17).

## 8. Malformed ABI rejection in ingress — confirmed intact

`authenticateV3Ingress` (v3-live.ts:4079-4140) rejects before `handleV3Ingress` ever runs: non-canonical envelope bytes (`V3Envelope.decode` + re-encode byte equality, 4104-4109), undetachable preimage/signature (4110-4115), `extractAuthorizedV3Vertex` throwing or returning undefined/not-ok (4122-4138 → `malformed-input` / reason), and `authenticatedRecoveryVertex` returning undefined (4139-4140). `isControlOperation` at 3910 only sees an already canonically decoded, authorized vertex. Local issuance likewise validates via `detachedCanonicalOperation` (6087-6095, used at 6238) and reducer existence (6258).

## 9. Call-site audit — all `isControlOperation(` sites pass a profileId

Definition at 3502; call sites at **3910, 5540, 5588, 5619, 5714, 5741, 5836, 6301, 6770, 6799** — grep confirms every one passes either `registration.payload.trust.trust.profileId` or `payload.trust.trust.profileId`. No stale single-argument call remains, and no call site passes a non-authenticated profile source.

## Defects noticed

None. Minor observations only:
- Line 1469 defensively wraps `String(trust.profileId)` while the new `isControlOperation` call sites pass `trust.profileId` directly — harmless, since `settlementProfileFor` is an exact string equality and a non-string would simply yield `"none"` (fail toward application treatment, and fence ops are separately gated by `isAuthorFenceOperation` + profile checks at 3906/5585/5738/6248/6588).
- The settlement-v1 `acl`-intent asymmetry noted in item 6 appears deliberate (mirrors the `displacedAction === "acl"` allowance in both `validRebaseRow` and the displaced-recovery path at 5711-5714).

